Bridge injected platform tags into the imported .veg config.

CUE injects tags into entrypoint package files, but not imported dependency
packages. Without this bridge, local and OS-only binary variants retain
non-concrete GOOS and GOARCH values.

Applied to copy.sh output before rewrite.sh. Idempotent via patch --forward.
The explicit config import alias survives the subsequent package rename.
--- a/envs.cue
+++ b/envs.cue
@@ -1,10 +1,19 @@
 package hof
 
 import (
-	"github.com/hofstadter-io/hof/.veg:veg"
+	config "github.com/hofstadter-io/hof/.veg:veg"
 )
 
-veg
+let root = self
+
+// CUE only injects tags into entrypoint packages, not imported packages.
+// Bridge the platform tags into the imported repo configuration.
+veg: config & {
+	flags: {
+		goos: root.flags.goos
+		arch: root.flags.arch
+	}
+}
 
 flags: {
 	// TODO, scope these since we are now injecting the entire package at the repo root
